      "title": "Improper Input Validation in io.undertow:undertow-core",
      "description": "Affected versions of io.undertow:undertow-core are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation. When Undertow parses large application/x-www-form-urlencoded bodies via FormEncodedDataDefinition.doParse(StreamSourceChannel), it can allocate unbounded buffers and run out of memory, allowing a remote attacker to trigger an OutOfMemoryError and cause a denial-of-service.",
